":"Local and general anesthetics","q":[{"s":"Which local anesthetic is an amide?","o":["Chloroprocaine","Cocaine","Tetracaine","Lidocaine","Benzocaine"],"e":["Wrong. Ester.","Wrong. Ester.","Wrong. Ester.","Correct. Amides have two i's in their names.","Wrong. Ester."],"a":3,"p":"565","k":"Local anesthetics"},{"s":"A patient allergic to procaine-type esters needs a local anesthetic. Which should be chosen?","o":["Bupivacaine","Tetracaine","Chloroprocaine","Cocaine","Benzocaine"],"e":["Correct. If allergic to esters, give amides.","Wrong. Ester.","Wrong. Ester.","Wrong. Ester.","Wrong. Ester."],"a":0,"p":"565","k":"Local anesthetics"},{"s":"Local anesthetics block conduction by binding:","o":["K+ channels on the outer membrane","Nicotinic receptors","Ligand-gated Cl− channels","The inner portion of voltage-gated Na+ channels","Ca2+ channels at the NMJ"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":3,"p":"565","k":"Local anesthetics"},{"s":"Why is more local anesthetic needed to drain an abscess?","o":["Acidic tissue charges the anesthetic, so it cannot penetrate the membrane","Bacteria degrade the drug","Inflammation increases blood flow only","Neurons fire less","The drug is bound by pus"],"e":["Correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not the listed reason.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":0,"p":"565","k":"Local anesthetics"},{"s":"Epinephrine is added to lidocaine to:","o":["Speed metabolism","Prolong the block by reducing systemic absorption","Prevent methemoglobinemia","Reduce pain of injection","Increase systemic absorption"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Opposite."],"a":1,"p":"565","k":"Local anesthetics"},{"s":"Local anesthetics block sensation in which order?","o":["Pressure, touch, temperature, pain","Temperature, pressure, pain, touch","Touch, pain, pressure, temperature","All at once","Pain, temperature, touch, pressu